{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{1}]+{a}_{2}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{2}]+{a}_{3}^{2}\\text{Var}[{X}_{3}] \\\\  & +2{a}_{1}{a}_{2}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{2}]+2{a}_{1}{a}_{3}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{1},{X}_{3}]+2{a}_{2}{a}_{3}\\text{Cov}[{X}_{2},{X}_{3}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3{X}_{1}+2{X}_{2}+4{X}_{3}] & ={3}^{2}\\cdot 5+{2}^{2}\\cdot 4+{4}^{2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & +2\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 3\\cdot 4\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 2\\cdot 4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =45+16+32+36+24+32 \\\\  & =185.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188786 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186186996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188786 #edb/ref 1069 "q-148162" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188786 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188786 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider two random variables $X$ and $Y$ with expectations $\\text{E}[X]=2,$ $\\text{E}[Y]=4,$ mixed moment $\\text{E}[XY]=10,$ and second raw moments $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=9$ and $\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]=20.$ Find the variance of $2X-5Y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188786 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bf786f34-fcab-562f-85da-9ff62292e23b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188786 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188786 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2},\n$$\n\nand the covariance of two random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find $\\text{Var}[X]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =9-{2}^{2} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =20-{4}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =10-2\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2X-5Y] & ={2}^{2}\\cdot 5+(-5)^{2}\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 2\\cdot (-5)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =20+100-40 \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188787 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186187002 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188787 #edb/ref 1069 "q-148163" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188787 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188787 #edb/ref 1071 "The joint probability mass function of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.5$ |\n\nFind $\\text{Var}[2X+3Y].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188787 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aa43e91a-459b-5961-9f5d-0107414a7dce" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188787 #edb/ref 1073 true #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186188787 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y]+2ab\\,\\text{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nAlso, the variance of a random variable $X$ is determined by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2},\n$$\n\nand the covariance of two random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\text{Cov}[X,Y]=\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y].\n$$\n\nFirst, let's find the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y.$ These are given by the row and column totals, respectively.\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.5$ | $0.8$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nNow, we can find $\\text{Var}[X].$ If $X$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{X},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}x\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.2+1\\cdot 0.8 \\\\  & =0.8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in {S}_{X}}{x}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{X}(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{2}\\cdot 0.2+{1}^{2}\\cdot 0.8 \\\\  & =0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =0.8-{0.8}^{2} \\\\  & =0.16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, if $Y$ is defined on a sample space ${S}_{Y},$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[Y] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}y\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0.4+2\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =1.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{y\\in {S}_{y}}{y}^{2}\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y) \\\\  & ={1}^{2}\\cdot 0.4+{2}^{2}\\cdot 0.6 \\\\  & =2.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y] & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}]-\\text{E}[Y]^{2} \\\\  & =2.8-{1.6}^{2} \\\\  & =0.24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's find $\\text{Cov}[X,Y].$ We compute $\\text{E}[XY]$ using the rule of the lazy statistician:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}xy\\cdot f(x,y) \\\\  & =0\\cdot 1\\cdot f(0,1)+0\\cdot 2\\cdot f(0,2)+1\\cdot 1\\cdot f(1,1)+1\\cdot 2\\cdot f(1,2) \\\\  & =0+0+1\\cdot 0.3+2\\cdot 0.5 \\\\  & =1.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the covariance formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[XY] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =1.3-0.8\\cdot 1.6 \\\\  & =0.02.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[2X+3Y] & ={2}^{2}\\cdot 0.16+{3}^{2}\\cdot 0.24+2\\cdot 2\\cdot 3\\cdot 0.02 \\\\  & =0.64+2.16+0.24 \\\\  & =3.04.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189207 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189208 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189207 #edb/ref 1061 39341 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189207 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "91e3c205-114c-5ae0-8abd-5bb7f424476e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189207 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186189413 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189208 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189211 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189208 #edb/ref 1061 39343 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189208 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8ceb42c5-5f3d-52e4-b3c8-bda0bdf99ba6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189208 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186188357 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189210 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189212 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189210 #edb/ref 1061 39369 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189210 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "982300e3-8874-58e0-b502-0dd1759d2e87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189210 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186188359 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189211 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189211 #edb/ref 1061 39370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189211 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8153054a-c500-5f13-a328-66eb26fc4fb8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189211 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186189414 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189212 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189222 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189212 #edb/ref 1061 39371 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189212 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ba8e9c50-818a-52c4-8395-b662c6ac186d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189212 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186188360 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189213 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189223 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189213 #edb/ref 1061 39377 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189213 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5fad4c43-2456-5538-bc40-e43bafabf67e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189213 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186188361 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189222 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186189213 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189222 #edb/ref 1061 39481 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189222 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "63b7b972-cc52-5658-b0d3-7a5571d28c29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189222 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186189420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189223 #edb/ref 1061 39482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189223 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9262448d-d4d1-5e9c-a798-bcc9d934f487" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189223 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186189421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189413 #edb/ref 1064 "Given two random variables $X$ and $Y,$ the variance of the sum or difference of these variables is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X\\pm Y] = \\textrm{Var}[X] + \\textrm{Var}[Y] \\pm 2\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y],\n$$\n\nwhere $\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance of $X$ and $Y.$ We'll prove this formula at the end of the lesson.\n\nNote that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent, then $\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y]= 0,$ and we have\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X\\pm Y] = \\textrm{Var}[X] + \\textrm{Var}[Y].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189413 #edb/ref 1065 6496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189413 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "84bffdf5-551d-52b7-93f3-5c7ba599e972" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189413 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189414 #edb/ref 1064 "If $X$ and $Y$ are random variables and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[aX + bY] = a^2 \\textrm{Var}[X] + b^2 \\textrm{Var}[Y] + 2ab \\textrm{Cov}[X,Y].\n$$\n\nIf $X$ and $Y$ are independent, then $\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y] = 0,$ and we recover the formula\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[aX + bY] = a^2 \\textrm{Var}[X] + b^2 \\textrm{Var}[Y] .\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189414 #edb/ref 1065 6502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189414 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a2319f43-f4e9-5092-93cf-5e5f4f23f4f7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189414 #edb/ref 1067 "The Variance of a Sum of Scaled Random Variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189420 #edb/ref 1064 "Finally, we have the following generalization for the variance of a sum of $n$ random variables.\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var} \\left[ \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^{n} a_i X_i \\right] = \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^{n} a_i^2 \\textrm{Var}[X_i] + 2\\sum\\limits_{i < j} a_i a_j \\textrm{Cov}[X_i, X_j]\n$$\n\nLet's see an example of how this works in practice." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189420 #edb/ref 1065 6535 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189420 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "5169e0a6-5da8-51b4-8e84-5154fe8622f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189420 #edb/ref 1067 "Generalizing to Multiple Random Variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189421 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's prove the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X+ Y] = \\textrm{Var}[X] + \\textrm{Var}[Y] + 2\\textrm{Cov}[X,Y]\n$$\n\nApplying the definition of variance and using the linearity of expectation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X+Y] & =\\text{E}[((X+Y)-\\text{E}[X+Y])^{2}] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[((X-\\text{E}[X])+(Y-\\text{E}[Y]))^{2}] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[(X-\\text{E}[X])^{2}+(Y-\\text{E}[Y])^{2}+2(X-\\text{E}[X])(Y-\\text{E}[Y])].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDistributing the expected value, and using the fact that $\\textrm{E}[aX] = a\\cdot \\textrm{E}[X]$ for constant $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X+Y] & =\\text{E}[(X-\\text{E}[X])^{2}+(Y-\\text{E}[Y])^{2}+2(X-\\text{E}[X])(Y-\\text{E}[Y])] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[(X-\\text{E}[X])^{2}]+\\text{E}[(Y-\\text{E}[Y])^{2}]+2\\cdot \\text{E}[(X-\\text{E}[X])(Y-\\text{E}[Y])] \\\\  & =\\text{Var}[X]+\\text{Var}[Y]+2\\text{Cov}[X,Y]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nas required. \n\nThe proof for the difference between two random variables is similar." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189421 #edb/ref 1065 6536 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189421 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7523c9e9-51f7-52f5-b206-eec1940bf0f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186189421 #edb/ref 1067 "Proof of the Sum Formula" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526510 #edb/ref 1080 "83" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526510 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526510 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "042d7ca6-0980-5b74-8fb1-e853458aefff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526517 #edb/ref 1080 "9.63" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526517 #edb/r